  "description": "Count valid lines by log level. A valid line has the form `YYYY-MM-DD [LEVEL] message`, where LEVEL is INFO, WARN, or ERROR and message is non-empty. Ignore malformed lines and return all three levels with zero counts when absent.",
  "starterCode": "def summarize_log_levels(lines):\n    # Return counts for INFO, WARN, and ERROR\n    pass\n",
  "referenceSolution": "import re\n\ndef summarize_log_levels(lines):\n    counts = {\"INFO\": 0, \"WARN\": 0, \"ERROR\": 0}\n    pattern = re.compile(r\"\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2} \\[(INFO|WARN|ERROR)\\] .+\")\n    for line in lines:\n        match = pattern.fullmatch(line)\n        if match:\n            counts[match.group(1)] += 1\n    return counts",
  "solution": {
    "code": "import re\n\ndef summarize_log_levels(lines):\n    counts = {\"INFO\": 0, \"WARN\": 0, \"ERROR\": 0}\n    pattern = re.compile(r\"\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2} \\[(INFO|WARN|ERROR)\\] .+\")\n    for line in lines:\n        match = pattern.fullmatch(line)\n        if match:\n            counts[match.group(1)] += 1\n    return counts",
    "explanation": "Match each complete line against the expected date, level, and message shape. Count only valid lines and ignore malformed entries. The regex anchors prevent a valid fragment from making an invalid line count."
  },
  "wrongSolutions": [
